abstract: >-
  OCTooL is a comprehensive software application designed for the export,
  analysis, and quantification of Optical Coherence Tomography (OCT)
  images. It provides researchers and clinicians with powerful tools to
  extract quantitative data from OCT imaging studies, including batch
  processing, interactive annotation, and advanced lesion depth detection
  algorithms.
keywords:
  - OCT
  - optical coherence tomography
  - image analysis
  - quantitative analysis
  - lesion depth
  - dental research
  - medical imaging
  - Python
  - tkinter
repository-code: "https://github.com/T0bC/OCTooL.git"
version: 2026.7
date-released: 2026-08-20
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
notes: >-
  Tobias Meißner is the main developer and maintainer of OCTooL, and led
  architecture and development across all modules (RexView, AnnoLyze,
  CarlQuant), GUI design, error handling, documentation, and release
  management. Hartmut Schneider, Rainer Haak, and Ellen Schulz-Kornas
  contributed to the study conception, dental research context, and
  manuscript preparation underlying the associated publication.

  Acknowledgments: Maximilian Bemmann (former member of the Leipzig
  University working group) implemented the initial CarlQuant prototype
  in MATLAB. Jonas Golde (Fraunhofer Institute for Material and Beam
  Technology (IWS), Technische Universität Dresden) provided the
  foundational OCT spectral-to-grayvalue conversion algorithm
  (originally implemented in MATLAB) that underpins the RexView module's
  image reconstruction logic, developed during the joint Inno-Fill
  project.

  Generative AI tools were used to assist with code generation,
  debugging, and documentation drafting during the development of this
  software. The authors reviewed all AI-generated content for
  correctness, functionality, and scientific accuracy and take full
  responsibility for the final published work. The following model(s) or
  application(s) were used: Claude Sonnet 4.6, Claude Opus 4.5, Kimi 2.5.
